## Step 2: Create synthetic JSONL fixture

Create `tests/fixtures/threading-session.jsonl` — a realistic CC conversation log with 12-15 events.

The fixture must use the ACTUAL Claude Code JSONL format. Each line is a JSON object with fields: `type`, `uuid`, `parentUuid`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `isSidechain`.

For `user` type events:
```json
{"type":"user","uuid":"u-001","parentUuid":"prev-uuid","isSidechain":false,"timestamp":"2026-05-20T10:00:00.000Z","sessionId":"test-session","message":{"role":"user","content":"the user message text"},"userType":"external","cwd":"/project","version":"2.1.0"}
```

For `assistant` type events (can have multiple content blocks):
```json
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"a-001","parentUuid":"u-001","isSidechain":false,"timestamp":"2026-05-20T10:00:05.000Z","sessionId":"test-session","message":{"role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_001","type":"message","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll check the auth middleware..."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"tu-001","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/project/src/auth.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"tu-002","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/project/src/auth.ts","old_string":"old","new_string":"new"}}]}}
